{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYvmxmR8gvPG9kL7Nck","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the new limits OpenAI announced for ChatGPT directs the model to give less detailed information about past mass attacks and the people who carried them out, \"even if it is available from other online sources.\" That sets aside a test often applied to sensitive questions, whether the facts are already public, and replaces it with a question about what the answer would do, such as reconstruct an attack.\n\nOpenAI says ChatGPT should still help people understand these events, learn how victims and communities were affected, and recognize warning signs and prevent future violence. The tightening applies to reconstructions of past attacks, including details about the weapons and equipment used and how they were obtained, and to detailed comparisons of scale of harm that could amplify an attacker's notoriety. The company states that these limits apply regardless of a user's age or reason for asking, so a stated purpose does not change the boundary.\n\nThis extends past what the company says its models already do, which is refuse to give instructions that would help someone plan or carry out violence. The new restriction covers descriptions of events that have already happened, a category where the same details can serve a student writing about an attack and someone fixated on one. The announcement does not say how the line between understanding an event and reconstructing it will be drawn in practice, or how much detail ChatGPT will now leave out.\n\nThat gap may narrow with the first Community Safety Report, due in early 2027. OpenAI says it will include anonymized examples of how violence-related harm shows up in its systems, along with new mitigations and policy changes. The safeguards themselves are set to begin rolling out within weeks of the October 30 announcement, which means users will see the new boundaries well before any published examples explain them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1366,"cache_read_input_tokens":4803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1366},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16675d8d-fb07-4158-9574-927ab2753178","uuid":"9f0bbccf-1244-4450-a1c7-a5563d645a4b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:30:07.098Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYvmitPET15LsykgYiP"}
